  "ownership": [
    "Trace copies only outer arrays and retains original Arc state/message identities. Pure recording, breadcrumbs and explicit-comparator replay impose no Clone, Send, serde or static bounds on model values.",
    "Runtime factories attach through the existing ordered/deduplicated retained observation owner, using Weak callbacks and explicit stop. The native Recorder handle also detaches on Drop as Rust resource cleanup.",
    "Update-only replay calls the existing core fold_msgs_shared loop. It does not init, interpret commands, touch stores, or select subscriptions.",
    "JSON serialization/parse codecs are explicit at wire boundaries. Typed callback causes and rejected raw input/physical line survive as data.",
    "JSONL uses the canonical decode_json_text and one shared JS whitespace predicate extracted unchanged from js_record string-number trimming. Existing number/string/property pub(crate) visibility for the DO owner is preserved.",
    "No parser, scheduler, Promise, schema, registry or DI engine added. Native runtime composition uses the existing executor and both profiles."
  ],
  "preservedSourceDetails": [
    "Final state advances even for dropped samples; rate one never samples; NaN RNG keeps a sample. Reentrant sampling records inner before outer and preserves the actual latest endpoint.",
    "Optional captureSteps presence, null/undefined boot and missing-anchor refusal, honest sampled endpoint, stop/idempotence, and fresh dump arrays retain source behavior.",
    "No trailing JSONL newline. Steps are positional when present, including empty/short arrays; null interior states only when steps are absent. Sparse parsed steps intentionally shift on rewrite, matching the source.",
    "Blank lines and exact JS trim retain physical line numbering. Missing state is known undefined, null tails retain the last known state, duplicate/missing boot and unusable null anchor are refused.",
    "Structural comparison uses Object.is including NaN and signed zero, UTF16-sorted own-key union, inherited pristine Object.prototype reads, array-node length mismatch and unchanged dotted/index path grammar."
  ],
